   "widgets_values": [
    "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the white dragon-armored knight in <Picture 1>: a tall humanoid figure in segmented ivory-white ceramic armor plated with polished gold, a dragon-head helm with swept-back horns and narrow eye slits glowing warm amber, overlapping scale plates across the chest, a black chainmail underlayer visible at the neck, waist and inner thighs, gold-trimmed spiked pauldrons, and articulated gold-banded gauntlets.\n<Subject 2> is the cathedral-like hall in <Picture 1>: a vast interior of fluted stone columns wrapped in gilded relief and arched galleries, one broad shaft of pale daylight falling from high above, fine dust suspended in the air, and a large crystal sphere on a gold mount at the right edge of frame, rendered with heavy background defocus.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] The target video holds <Subject 1> standing in <Subject 2> under a single overhead shaft of light, then moves from a low-angle medium shot into a tight chest-up arc as the helm's amber eye glow intensifies. The armor and hall come from <Picture 1>, and no dialogue is spoken.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): fully_preserved - the ivory-white and gold dragon armor, the horned helm, the amber eye glow, the black chainmail underlayer and the spiked pauldrons are retained.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): partially_preserved - the gilded fluted columns, the overhead light shaft, the drifting dust and the crystal sphere are retained while the background falls further out of focus as the camera closes in.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is rendered with photoreal hard-surface detail: polished ceramic and gold carrying fine micro-scratches, cool silver-blue fill light from the left, warm gold backlight from the shaft above, and a shallow depth of field that keeps the armor sharp while the hall dissolves into soft bokeh.\n[Shot 1] A low-angle medium shot from slightly below chest height establishes <Subject 2>: tall fluted columns sheathed in gilded relief rise out of focus on both sides, and one broad shaft of pale daylight falls from high above, filling the air with drifting dust. <Subject 1>, the white dragon-armored knight, stands just left of center in three-quarter view, the horned helm turned toward the upper left and catching a thin rim of light along its swept horns. The camera moves in a slow, steady dolly-in with a slight upward tilt, small in amplitude and gradual in speed, closing about one third of the framing distance over three seconds. The dust motes slide past in slow parallax. The amber glow inside the helm's eye slits pulses once, brightening then settling. The knight's chest rises in a single slow, deep breath and the layered scale plates shift a few millimeters against each other. Gold trim on the pauldrons flares and dulls as the camera angle crosses the reflection, and the crystal sphere at the right edge holds a soft bloom of light.\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.200, the shot cuts to a chest-up framing of <Subject 1>, the helm's horn tips nearly touching the top of frame. The camera arcs slowly to the right in a lateral move of medium amplitude, revealing the shoulder line in silhouette against the light shaft. The knight's right gauntlet lifts and the fingers close into a slow fist, the gold banding at each knuckle catching individual highlights. The amber eye glow brightens steadily and spills a faint warm reflection onto the gold brow ridge and the scales below. The head turns a few degrees toward camera and the helm's jaw plate edges into profile. The camera settles as the fist tightens fully, dust keeps drifting through the beam, and the frame holds on the horned profile with the hall reduced to floating bokeh and one flare from the crystal sphere.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA wide reverberant cathedral room tone with a low continuous airflow, faint metallic resonance from the gilded surfaces, one distant water drip with a long decay, and close, subtle scale-against-scale friction plus a single deep breath from inside the armor; no voices.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA sustained low brass drone on a single root note, joined by a sparse wordless low choir that swells slowly through the final two seconds and cuts off with the last frame; no percussion.\n"
   ]
